---
import SystemPage from '../../components/v2/SystemPage.astro';
import { imagery } from '../../content/imagery';

const v2 = imagery.v2;
---

<SystemPage
	title="EPDM commercial roofing"
	heroEyebrow="Commercial · single-ply"
	heroHeading="EPDM rubber.<br />The original single-ply."
	heroLede="Black synthetic-rubber membrane. 50+ year proven track record. Cold-weather installable. The right call for the right building — we tell you when that's the case."
	heroPhoto={v2.pageHeros.epdmRoofing}
	bleedPhoto={v2.bleeds.commercial}
	bleedHeading="Synthetic rubber.<br />Decades of field history."
	overview={{
		eyebrow: 'What EPDM is',
		heading: 'Vulcanized synthetic rubber, in big sheets.',
		body: "EPDM (ethylene propylene diene monomer) is a black synthetic-rubber membrane installed in sheets up to 50 ft wide with seam tape or bonding adhesive at the overlaps. It's the original single-ply system — in commercial use since the 1960s — and the longest field history of any membrane on the market. The trade-off versus TPO is reflectivity: EPDM is dark and absorbs heat where TPO reflects it."
	}}
	keyPoints={[
		{
			heading: 'Where EPDM is still the right call.',
			body: "EPDM still wins for cold-climate buildings, heating-dominated structures, and re-roof scenarios where the existing roof is EPDM and the tear-off math doesn't pencil. It also wins on raw longevity — the 50+ year service-life record on EPDM is real.",
			bullets: ['Heating-dominated buildings', 'Cold-climate installs (no minimum substrate temp)', 'Existing-EPDM re-cover candidates', '50+ year proven track record'],
			photo: v2.systemTiles.epdm,
			photoSide: 'left',
		},
		{
			heading: 'How it gets installed.',
			body: "Three main methods. Mechanically-attached is the fastest and lowest-cost. Fully-adhered uses bonding adhesive across the whole surface for high wind-uplift performance. Ballasted (river rock or pavers) is mostly historical but still in service on a lot of 1990s-era buildings.",
			bullets: ['Mechanically-attached (fastest)', 'Fully-adhered (high uplift)', 'Ballasted (mostly legacy at this point)'],
			photo: v2.bleeds.workmanship,
			photoSide: 'right',
		},
	]}
	stats={[
		{ value: '50+', label: 'Years field history' },
		{ value: '20–30', label: 'Years typical warranty' },
		{ value: '40°F', label: 'Min ambient temp · adhered' },
		{ value: 'Class A', label: 'Fire rating · ballasted UL 790' },
	]}
	projectPhotos={[v2.projects[5], v2.projects[7], v2.projects[6], v2.projects[3]]}
	projectCaptions={['EPDM re-roof, manufacturing', 'EPDM with ballast removal, Tyler', 'Adhered EPDM, healthcare', 'EPDM-to-TPO conversion bid']}
	faq={[
		{ q: 'Why would I pick EPDM over TPO in 2026?', a: "<p>If your existing roof is EPDM and structurally sound, sticking with EPDM avoids tear-off cost and lets us spot-repair instead of full replacement. If you're in a heating-dominated building (rare in East Texas, common in Arkansas hill country), the dark surface helps in winter. Otherwise, TPO is usually the answer.</p>" },
		{ q: 'How long does EPDM actually last?', a: '<p>50+ years documented in real-world installs. The membrane itself doesn\'t fail — what fails is seam tape, flashings, and ballast scour at edges. Maintained, an EPDM roof outlasts most of the buildings it\'s on.</p>' },
		{ q: 'Can you install EPDM in winter?', a: '<p>Yes — mechanically-attached EPDM has no temperature minimum. Adhered installs need substrate above ~40°F for the bonding adhesive. Ballasted installs run year-round.</p>' },
		{ q: 'What\'s the warranty?', a: '<p>Manufacturer warranties on EPDM run 20–30 years. Heritage adds a workmanship warranty on the install. Specific tier and length lands on the proposal once we know the system and the warranty path Heritage carries with that manufacturer.</p>' },
		{ q: 'Will it leak in 10 years?', a: '<p>If installed correctly and the seams are properly tape- or adhesive-bonded, no. EPDM leaks where the seams are weak or the flashings around penetrations have failed. Heritage installs all seams to manufacturer spec and the warranty covers them.</p>' },
	]}
	ctaHeading="EPDM walkthrough,<br />scope, and bid in a week."
	ctaLede="Free roof assessment. We tell you whether EPDM still makes sense for your building."
	ctaPhoto={v2.pageHeros.commercial}
/>
